         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>A short Gǝʿǝz theological treatise which is
              a translation from Arabic. In the early Church this kind
              of text was recited for the baptized faithful after the catechumens had been dismissed.
               Whilst <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</t:persName>, as the central celebrated ﬁgure,
               was described and praised without his name being mentioned directly,
               the initiated in the mysteries of the Christian faith knew who was intended.</t:p>
               
               <t:p>Not to be confused with the text also known as <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2444Temher">Tǝmhǝrta ḫǝbuʾāt</t:ref>.
               For the texts in the version than cannot be immediately identified, see
               <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT6688TeachingMysteries">Teaching of Mysteries (general record)</t:ref>.</t:p>
         </t:abstract>
